</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Living in a tilted world: climate change and geography limit speciation in Old World anchovies (Engraulis: Engraulidae)</article-title><source>Biological Journal of the Linnean Society</source><year>2006</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>673</fpage><lpage>689</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1095-8312.2006.00651.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pichler</surname><given-names>FB</given-names></name><name><surname>Robineau</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodall</surname><given-names>RNP</given-names></name><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Olavarria</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Baker</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Origin and radiation of Southern Hemisphere coastal dolphins (genus Cephalorhynchus)</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2001</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>2215</fpage><lpage>2223</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11555263</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.0962-1083.2001.01360.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cassens</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Warebeek</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Crespo</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Reyes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The phylogeography of dusky dolphins (Lagenorhynchus obscurus): a critical examination of network methods and rooting procedures</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2003</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>1781</fpage><lpage>1792</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">